I'm pretty sure that's not the case -- pets in nethack don't remember
their (current or former) owner's name.  (Former pets found on bones
levels are likely to be hostile until retamed, but this has nothing to
do with the player's name.)

I believe (though please do correct me if I'm wrong) that the only
case in which having the same name as the player who left the bones
file matters is if there was an angry shopkeeper on the level; the
shopkeeper will remain angry only if your name matches that of the
player who originally angered him/her.

